{"task_id": "HumanEval/1", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef separate_paren_groups(paren_string: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Separates groups of nested parentheses from a string, ignoring spaces and returning a list of balanced groups.\n    Groups are identified and separated at the top level when the nesting depth returns to zero.\n    >>> separate_paren_groups('( ) (( )) (( )( ))')\n    ['()', '(())', '(()())']\n    >>> separate_paren_groups('()()()')\n    ['()', '()', '()']\n    >>> separate_paren_groups('')\n    []\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    current_group = \"\"\n    depth = 0\n\n    for char in paren_string:\n        if char == ' ':\n            continue\n\n        if char == '(':\n            depth += 1\n            current_group += char\n        elif char == ')':\n            current_group += char\n            depth -= 1\n            if depth == 0:\n                result.append(current_group)\n                current_group = \"\"\n\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/1", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef separate_paren_groups(paren_string: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Separates multiple groups of nested parentheses into individual balanced strings, ignoring spaces. Groups are balanced and not nested within each other, returned in original order.\n    >>> separate_paren_groups('( ) (( )) (( )( ))')\n    ['()', '(())', '(()())']\n    \"\"\"\n    result: List[str] = []\n    nesting_level: int = 0\n    current_group: List[str] = []\n\n    for char in paren_string:\n        if char == ' ':\n            continue\n        elif char == '(':\n            current_group.append(char)\n            nesting_level += 1\n        elif char == ')':\n            current_group.append(char)\n            nesting_level -= 1\n\n            if nesting_level == 0:\n                result.append(''.join(current_group))\n                current_group = []\n\n    return result\n```"}
