{"task_id": "HumanEval/8", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Tuple\n\n\ndef sum_product(numbers: List[int]) -> Tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"Calculate the sum and product of all integers in the input list.\n    For an empty list, returns (0, 1).\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    total_product = 1\n\n    if not numbers:\n        return (0, 1)\n\n    for number in numbers:\n        total_sum += number\n        total_product *= number\n\n    return (total_sum, total_product)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/4", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef mean_absolute_deviation(numbers: List[float]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the Mean Absolute Deviation (MAD) for a list of numbers.\n    MAD is the average absolute difference between each element and the mean of the dataset.\n    \"\"\"\n    mean = sum(numbers) / len(numbers)\n    sum_differences = sum(abs(x - mean) for x in numbers)\n    mad = sum_differences / len(numbers)\n    return mad\n```"}
