{"task_id": "HumanEval/19", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_numbers(numbers: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Sorts space-delimited word numerals (zero-nine) in ascending numeric order.\n    Preserves word format in the space-delimited output string.\"\"\"\n\n    word_to_num_map = {\n        'zero': 0, 'one': 1, 'two': 2, 'three': 3, 'four': 4,\n        'five': 5, 'six': 6, 'seven': 7, 'eight': 8, 'nine': 9\n    }\n\n    # Split input by spaces and filter out any empty strings.\n    words = [word for word in numbers.split(' ') if word]\n\n    # Sort words using their numeric value as the key.\n    sorted_words = sorted(words, key=lambda word: word_to_num_map[word])\n\n    return ' '.join(sorted_words)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/29", "solution": "```python\ndef filter_by_prefix(strings: List[str], prefix: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\" Filter an input list of strings only for ones that start with a given prefix.\n    >>> filter_by_prefix([], 'a')\n    []\n    >>> filter_by_prefix(['abc', 'bcd', 'cde', 'array'], 'a')\n    ['abc', 'array']\n    \"\"\"\n    # Uses a list comprehension for O(n) performance and to create a new list.\n    # `str.startswith()` performs case-sensitive matching and preserves original order.\n    return [s for s in strings if s.startswith(prefix)]\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/29", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef filter_by_prefix(strings: List[str], prefix: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Filter a list of strings to return only those starting with a given prefix.\n    Returns a new list containing only matching strings, preserving original order.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not strings:\n        return []\n\n    result = []\n    for string in strings:\n        if string.startswith(prefix):\n            result.append(string)\n\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/27", "solution": "```python\ndef flip_case(string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\" For a given string, flip lowercase characters to uppercase and uppercase to lowercase.\n    >>> flip_case('Hello')\n    'hELLO'\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for char in string:\n        if char.isalpha():\n            if char.isupper():\n                result.append(char.lower())\n            else:  # char is alphabetic and is not upper, so it must be lower\n                result.append(char.upper())\n        else:\n            result.append(char)\n    return ''.join(result)\n```"}
