{"task_id": "HumanEval/31", "solution": "```python\ndef is_prime(n):\n    \"\"\"Return true if a given number is prime, and false otherwise.\n    >>> is_prime(6)\n    False\n    >>> is_prime(101)\n    True\n    >>> is_prime(11)\n    True\n    >>> is_prime(13441)\n    True\n    >>> is_prime(61)\n    True\n    >>> is_prime(4)\n    False\n    >>> is_prime(1)\n    False\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 2:\n        return False\n    if n == 2:\n        return True\n    if n % 2 == 0:  # Handle all even numbers greater than 2.\n        return False\n\n    # Check for odd divisors only up to the square root of n.\n    sqrt_n = int(n ** 0.5)\n    for divisor in range(3, sqrt_n + 1, 2):\n        if n % divisor == 0:\n            return False\n    return True\n```"}
