{"task_id": "HumanEval/44", "solution": "```python\ndef change_base(x: int, base: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Converts an integer x to its string representation in the specified base.\n    The base must be between 2 and 9, and the result uses only digit characters.\n    >>> change_base(8, 3)\n    '22'\n    >>> change_base(8, 2)\n    '1000'\n    >>> change_base(7, 2)\n    '111'\n    \"\"\"\n    if x == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n\n    is_negative = (x < 0)\n    x = abs(x)\n\n    digits = []\n    while x > 0:\n        remainder = x % base\n        digits.append(remainder)\n        x = x // base\n\n    digits.reverse()\n\n    result_string = \"\".join(str(d) for d in digits)\n    if is_negative:\n        result_string = \"-\" + result_string\n\n    return result_string\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "```python\ndef fib4(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"The Fib4 number sequence. Computes the n-th element iteratively with O(1) space.\n    Each element (for n>=4) is the sum of the four preceding elements, with specific base cases.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Handle base cases for n < 4\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 3:\n        return 0\n    # Compute iteratively for n >= 4 using a sliding window\n    else:\n        # Initialize the sliding window with base values fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3)\n        v0, v1, v2, v3 = 0, 0, 2, 0\n\n        # Iterate from n=4 up to the desired n\n        for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n            next_fib = v0 + v1 + v2 + v3\n            # Shift the window: discard oldest, add newest\n            v0 = v1\n            v1 = v2\n            v2 = v3\n            v3 = next_fib\n\n        # The last value in the window (v3) is fib4(n)\n        return v3\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "```python\ndef fib4(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute the n-th element of the Fib4 sequence iteratively.\n    It uses O(n) time and O(1) space complexity by maintaining a sliding window of the last four values.\n    >>> fib4(5)\n    4\n    >>> fib4(6)\n    8\n    >>> fib4(7)\n    14\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n    if n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    fib0, fib1, fib2, fib3 = 0, 0, 2, 0  # Initialize with fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3)\n\n    for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n        new_val = fib0 + fib1 + fib2 + fib3\n        fib0, fib1, fib2, fib3 = fib1, fib2, fib3, new_val\n\n    return fib3\n```"}
