{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import Union\n\n\ndef median(l: list) -> Union[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    The list is sorted, and the median is calculated based on its length parity.\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_list = _sort_numbers(l)\n    length = len(sorted_list)\n\n    if length % 2 == 1:  # Odd length\n        return _get_middle_element(sorted_list)\n    else:  # Even length\n        return _get_average_of_middle_elements(sorted_list)\n\n\ndef _sort_numbers(numbers: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Create a sorted copy of the input list in ascending order.\n    The original list remains unmodified.\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_list = numbers.copy()\n    sorted_list.sort()\n    return sorted_list\n\n\ndef _get_middle_element(sorted_list: list) -> Union[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"Get the middle element from a sorted odd-length list.\n    The middle index is calculated using integer division.\n    \"\"\"\n    middle_index = len(sorted_list) // 2\n    return sorted_list[middle_index]\n\n\ndef _get_average_of_middle_elements(sorted_list: list) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculate the average of two middle elements from a sorted even-length list.\n    The result is always a float to maintain precision.\n    \"\"\"\n    middle_index_1 = len(sorted_list) // 2 - 1\n    middle_index_2 = len(sorted_list) // 2\n    elem1 = sorted_list[middle_index_1]\n    elem2 = sorted_list[middle_index_2]\n    return (elem1 + elem2) / 2.0\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/49", "solution": "```python\ndef modp(n: int, p: int):\n    \"\"\"Return 2^n modulo p using binary exponentiation.\n    Handles various edge cases like n=0, p=1, and negative n.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Validation: Modulo p must be positive.\n    if p <= 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # Edge case: 2^0 is 1.\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Edge case: Any number modulo 1 is 0.\n    if p == 1:\n        return 0\n\n    # Edge case: Negative exponents are not supported.\n    if n < 0:\n        return 0\n\n    result = 1\n    base = 2\n    exponent_copy = n\n\n    # Perform binary exponentiation (exponentiation by squaring).\n    while exponent_copy > 0:\n        if exponent_copy % 2 == 1:\n            result = (result * base) % p\n        base = (base * base) % p\n        exponent_copy //= 2  # Integer division for exponent.\n\n    return result\n```"}
