{"task_id": "HumanEval/57", "solution": "```python\ndef monotonic(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return True if list elements are monotonically increasing or decreasing.\n    This function implements a single-pass algorithm with O(n) time and O(1) space complexity.\"\"\"\n\n    if len(l) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    increasing = True\n    decreasing = True\n\n    for i in range(1, len(l)):\n        if l[i] > l[i-1]:\n            decreasing = False\n        elif l[i] < l[i-1]:\n            increasing = False\n\n        # Optimization: if neither increasing nor decreasing, it's non-monotonic\n        if not increasing and not decreasing:\n            return False\n\n    return increasing or decreasing\n```"}
