{"task_id": "HumanEval/65", "solution": "```python\ndef circular_shift(x, shift):\n    \"\"\"Circular shift the digits of the integer x, shift the digits right by shift\n    and return the result as a string. If shift > number of digits, return digits reversed.\n    >>> circular_shift(12, 1)\n    \"21\"\n    >>> circular_shift(12, 2)\n    \"12\"\n    \"\"\"\n    digit_string = str(abs(x))\n    digit_count = len(digit_string)\n\n    if shift > digit_count:\n        result = digit_string[::-1]\n    else:\n        normalized_shift = shift % digit_count\n        rotation_point = digit_count - normalized_shift\n        left_part = digit_string[:rotation_point]\n        right_part = digit_string[rotation_point:]\n        result = right_part + left_part\n\n    return result\n```"}
