{"task_id": "HumanEval/87", "solution": "```python\ndef get_row(lst, x):\n    \"\"\"\n    You are given a 2 dimensional data, as a nested lists,\n    which is similar to matrix, however, unlike matrices,\n    each row may contain a different number of columns.\n    Given lst, and integer x, find integers x in the list,\n    and return list of tuples, [(x1, y1), (x2, y2) ...] such that\n    each tuple is a coordinate - (row, columns), starting with 0.\n    Sort coordinates initially by rows in ascending order.\n    Also, sort coordinates of the row by columns in descending order.\n\n    Examples:\n    get_row([\n      [1,2,3,4,5,6],\n      [1,2,3,4,1,6],\n      [1,2,3,4,5,1]\n    ], 1) == [(0, 0), (1, 4), (1, 0), (2, 5), (2, 0)]\n    get_row([], 1) == []\n    get_row([[], [1], [1, 2, 3]], 3) == [(2, 2)]\n    \"\"\"\n    if not lst:\n        return []\n\n    results = []\n    for row_idx, row in enumerate(lst):\n        for col_idx, element in enumerate(row):\n            if element == x:\n                results.append((row_idx, col_idx))\n\n    sorted_results = sorted(results, key=lambda coord: (coord[0], -coord[1]))\n\n    return sorted_results\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/86", "solution": "```python\ndef anti_shuffle(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Transform a string by sorting characters within each word in ascending ASCII order.\n\n    Words are sequences of non-space characters separated by spaces.\n    Word order and all spaces are preserved.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Segment string into tokens (words and spaces)\n    tokens = _split_preserving_spaces(s)\n\n    # Process each token\n    result_tokens = []\n    for token_type, token_content in tokens:\n        if token_type == 'word':\n            result_tokens.append(_sort_word(token_content))\n        else:  # token_type == 'space'\n            result_tokens.append(token_content)\n\n    # Reconstruct and return result\n    return ''.join(result_tokens)\n\n\ndef _sort_word(word):\n    \"\"\"Sort characters in a word by Unicode code point.\"\"\"\n    return ''.join(sorted(word))\n\n\ndef _split_preserving_spaces(s):\n    \"\"\"Split string into (type, content) tokens, preserving exact space counts.\"\"\"\n    tokens = []\n    current_type = None\n    current_content = \"\"\n\n    for char in s:\n        if char == ' ':\n            if current_type == 'word':\n                tokens.append(('word', current_content))\n                current_content = char\n                current_type = 'space'\n            elif current_type == 'space':\n                current_content += char\n            else:  # current_type is None\n                current_content = char\n                current_type = 'space'\n        else:  # non-space character\n            if current_type == 'space':\n                tokens.append(('space', current_content))\n                current_content = char\n                current_type = 'word'\n            elif current_type == 'word':\n                current_content += char\n            else:  # current_type is None\n                current_content = char\n                current_type = 'word'\n\n    # Append final token if any content remains\n    if current