{"task_id": "HumanEval/88", "solution": "```python\ndef create_copy(array):\n    \"\"\"Create a new shallow copy of the input list.\"\"\"\n    return list(array)\n\ndef get_first_element(array):\n    \"\"\"Retrieve the first element of the list.\"\"\"\n    return array[0]\n\ndef get_last_element(array):\n    \"\"\"Retrieve the last element of the list.\"\"\"\n    return array[-1]\n\ndef is_empty(array):\n    \"\"\"Check if the list is empty.\"\"\"\n    return len(array) == 0\n\ndef is_single_element(array):\n    \"\"\"Check if the list contains exactly one element.\"\"\"\n    return len(array) == 1\n\ndef calculate_sum(first, last):\n    \"\"\"Calculate the sum of two integers.\"\"\"\n    return first + last\n\ndef is_odd(value):\n    \"\"\"Determine if an integer is odd.\"\"\"\n    return value % 2 != 0\n\ndef sort_ascending(elements):\n    \"\"\"Return a new list sorted in ascending order.\"\"\"\n    return sorted(elements)\n\ndef sort_descending(elements):\n    \"\"\"Return a new list sorted in descending order.\"\"\"\n    return sorted(elements, reverse=True)\n\ndef sort_array(array):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given an array of non-negative integers, return a copy of the given array after sorting,\n    you will sort the given array in ascending order if the sum( first index value, last index value) is odd,\n    or sort it in descending order if the sum( first index value, last index value) is even.\n    \"\"\"\n    if is_empty(array):\n        return []\n\n    if is_single_element(array):\n        return create_copy(array)\n\n    first = get_first_element(array)\n    last = get_last_element(array)\n    sum_value = calculate_sum(first, last)\n\n    if is_odd(sum_value):\n        return sort_ascending(array)\n    else:\n        return sort_descending(array)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/88", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_array(array):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given an array of non-negative integers, return a copy of the given array after sorting,\n    you will sort the given array in ascending order if the sum( first index value, last index value) is odd,\n    or sort it in descending order if the sum( first index value, last index value) is even.\n\n    Note:\n    * don't change the given array.\n\n    Examples:\n    * sort_array([]) => []\n    * sort_array([5]) => [5]\n    * sort_array([2, 4, 3, 0, 1, 5]) => [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\n    * sort_array([2, 4, 3, 0, 1, 5, 6]) => [6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1, 0]\n    \"\"\"\n    if not array:\n        return []\n\n    if len(array) == 1:\n        return array[:]\n\n    boundary_sum = array[0] + array[-1]\n\n    if boundary_sum % 2 == 1:\n        return sorted(array)\n    else:\n        return sorted(array, reverse=True)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/89", "solution": "```python\ndef encrypt(s):\n    \"\"\"Create a function encrypt that takes a string as an argument and\n    returns a string encrypted with the alphabet being rotated.\n    The alphabet should be rotated in a manner such that the letters\n    shift down by two multiplied to two places.\n    For example:\n    encrypt('hi') returns 'lm'\n    encrypt('asdfghjkl') returns 'ewhjklnop'\n    encrypt('gf') returns 'kj'\n    encrypt('et') returns 'ix'\n    \"\"\"\n    # Constants\n    SHIFT = 4\n    ALPHABET_SIZE = 26\n    LOWERCASE_A_ASCII = 97  # ord('a')\n\n    # Build result character by character\n    result = []\n\n    for char in s:\n        # Check if character is lowercase ASCII letter (a-z)\n        if 'a' <= char <= 'z':\n            # Encrypt lowercase letter\n            position = ord(char) - LOWERCASE_A_ASCII\n            new_position = (position + SHIFT) % ALPHABET_SIZE\n            new_char = chr(new_position + LOWERCASE_A_ASCII)\n            result.append(new_char)\n        else:\n            # Preserve non-lowercase characters unchanged\n            result.append(char)\n\n    # Join list into string and return\n    return ''.join(result)\n```"}
